# PID-Based Temperature Control System (ESP32 + DHT22 + Blynk)

A closed-loop PID (Proportional-Integral-Derivative) temperature control system built with an ESP32 microcontroller. The system reads real-time temperature from a DHT22 sensor and dynamically adjusts a PWM-controlled heating element to maintain a user-defined setpoint. Live monitoring and remote setpoint adjustment are done through a Blynk IoT dashboard. The project is developed and simulated entirely in the Wokwi simulator, running inside VS Code with PlatformIO, so no physical hardware is required.

## How It Works

DHT22 sensor → ESP32 (PID algorithm) → PWM-controlled heater (LED) → DHT22 feedback loop
↕
Blynk Cloud → Mobile app / Web dashboard (live monitoring + setpoint control)

1. The DHT22 sensor measures the current temperature.
2. The ESP32 calculates the error between the setpoint and the current temperature.
3. A PID algorithm computes a correction value from the error, using Proportional, Integral, and Derivative terms.
4. The correction value is sent as a PWM signal to the heating element (simulated with an LED).
5. The current temperature, setpoint, and heater output are all displayed live on the Blynk dashboard, with history tracked on a chart.
6. The setpoint can be changed remotely from the Blynk app, and the system reacts accordingly.

## What Is PID Control

A PID controller continuously calculates an error value (the difference between a desired setpoint and a measured value) and applies a correction based on three terms:

| Term | Role |
|---|---|
| **P (Proportional)** | Reacts to the current error — larger error produces a larger correction |
| **I (Integral)** | Accounts for the accumulated past error — eliminates steady-state offset |
| **D (Derivative)** | Reacts to the rate of change of the error — reduces overshoot |

```
Output = Kp × error + Ki × (sum of error) + Kd × (rate of change of error)
```

## Components Used

| Component | Purpose |
|---|---|
| ESP32 | Main controller with built-in WiFi, runs the PID algorithm |
| DHT22 | Measures the current temperature (feedback sensor) |
| LED + Resistor | Simulates the heating element, driven by a PWM signal |
| Blynk IoT | Mobile app and cloud dashboard for live monitoring and setpoint control |
| Wokwi | Online simulator (replaces real hardware) |
| PlatformIO (VS Code) | Development environment used to build and run the simulation |

## Circuit Connections

| From | To | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| DHT22 VCC | ESP32 3V3 | Power |
| DHT22 SDA | ESP32 GPIO 15 | Temperature data |
| DHT22 GND | ESP32 GND | Ground |
| ESP32 GPIO 25 | Resistor | PWM signal (heater control) |
| Resistor | LED anode | Current limiting |
| LED cathode | ESP32 GND | Ground |

