## Code Overview

| Part | What It Does |
|---|---|
| `computePID(currentTemp)` | Calculates the PID output from the current error, integral, and derivative |
| `BLYNK_WRITE(V1)` | Updates the setpoint whenever it is changed from the Blynk app |
| `analogWrite(HEATER_PIN, output)` | Sends the PID output as a PWM signal to the heater (LED) |
| Integral windup limit | Caps the integral term so it does not grow unbounded during large or prolonged errors |
| `timer.setInterval(2000L, controlLoop)` | Runs the sensor read + PID calculation + output cycle every 2 seconds |

## Important Note

Never upload your real Blynk Auth Token to a public repository. This project uses placeholders. Add your own token only on your computer or in Wokwi.

